{
"dur": 76.831,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 10.36,
"text": "The war became a test for the bigger war to come. Hitler and Mussolini sent planes, tanks and troops to Franco. Stalin sent weapons and advisers to the Republic.",
"end": 10.635
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 10.635,
"vo_start": 10.91,
"vo_end": 18.469,
"text": "Britain and France stayed out. But around thirty-five thousand volunteers from more than fifty countries came to fight for the Republic in the International Brigades.",
"end": 18.744
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 18.744,
"vo_start": 19.019,
"vo_end": 27.479,
"text": "On the twenty-sixth of April 1937, a Monday, market day, German planes of the Condor Legion bombed the Basque town of Guernica for hours.",
"end": 27.754
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 27.754,
"vo_start": 28.029,
"vo_end": 37.891,
"text": "Much of the town was destroyed. Hundreds were killed. A few weeks later Pablo Picasso painted Guernica, and it became the most famous anti-war picture ever made.",
"end": 38.166
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 38.166,
"vo_start": 38.441,
"vo_end": 49.241,
"text": "The Republic was fighting itself as well. Communists, socialists, anarchists and others wanted different futures. In Barcelona in 1937 they fought each other in the streets.",
"end": 49.516
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 49.516,
"vo_start": 49.791,
"vo_end": 57.95,
"text": "The English writer George Orwell was there as a volunteer. A sniper shot him through the throat. He survived and wrote Homage to Catalonia.",
"end": 58.225
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 58.225,
"vo_start": 58.5,
"vo_end": 69.01,
"text": "Slowly, Franco's better-organised side won. Barcelona fell in January 1939, and Madrid at the end of March. On the first of April 1939, Franco declared the war over.",
"end": 69.285
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 69.285,
"vo_start": 69.56,
"vo_end": 75.881,
"text": "Estimates of the dead range from about three hundred and fifty thousand to half a million. Around half a million people fled to France.",
"end": 76.831
}
],
